    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d608">

                <pb facs="0592" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 337.11/445</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gonzales to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-17T21:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1917, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 16, 2 p.m. There are Government troops stationed at each one these
                    places except Canet. C. C. Reasoner, American, who recently went to La Gloria to
                    bring mother Habana, reports protection given by Government to that section
                    showed calm apprehension. Trains run through Minas every day. I have not only
                    asked for protection for alarmed American colonies but where it was possible
                    physically to get protection have not rested till it was provided. Most of the
                    robbery was before communication could be established. Isolated houses will be
                    in danger while robber bands exist.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
